 "stability_across_3_runs": "worst per-query spread 0.0010 ms in BOTH modes across three runs per mode after a discarded warmup run per mode; node and edge counts identical across all three runs in both modes, and the cross-build query-result parity flag held on every cell of every run. FLOOR HELD AT 0.005 for the same reason 0.2.10 held it: three runs inside one warm window under-sample the cross-session jitter this corpus shows (0.2.9 saw 0.0020, and the 0.2.10 control re-measure saw a 0.002 ms spread), and 0.005 is 2.5x that evidence. Sixth baseline of the 0.2.6 corpus epoch (c449542e, 30 corpora). Control top20_by_branch_count re-qualified across the kglite 0.16.13->0.16.15 engine move: the release-gate anchor compare read it at +6.25% docs-on and +20% docs-off (+0.003 ms raw, under the floor) against the 0.2.8 baseline \u2014 sub-floor jitter, not a deterministic move \u2014 and this capture stores it at 0.015 ms in both modes, 3.0x the 0.005 floor, clear of the 2x margin (doctrine R11 corollary).",
